        <section class="content-section" id="overview">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="row align-items-center g-5">
                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                        <span class="section-eyebrow">Statutory Real Estate Governance</span>
                        <h2 class="section-h2">Understanding the RERA Legal Shield in Tamil Nadu</h2>
                        <p>
                            Investing in Indian residential and commercial real estate from abroad represents a major financial commitment for overseas Indians. However, NRIs frequently confront unscrupulous builders who leverage geographical distance to delay project handovers indefinitely, alter sanctioned building drawings, demand unauthorized financial escalations, or fail to deliver statutory completion certificates.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Enacted to eliminate asymmetrical builder dominance, the <strong>Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 (RERA Act)</strong> read with the <strong>Tamil Nadu Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules, 2017 (TNRERA Rules)</strong> creates a dedicated, fast-track statutory framework. Dispute adjudication is vested in specialized regulatory forums: the <strong>Tamil Nadu Real Estate Regulatory Authority (TNRERA)</strong>, the <strong>Adjudicating Officer</strong> for damages, and the <strong>Tamil Nadu Real Estate Appellate Tribunal (TNREAT)</strong>.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            At <strong>RRC Law Associates</strong>, our experienced real estate litigation advocates deliver comprehensive, zero-travel legal counsel to NRIs across North America, Europe, the Middle East, Southeast Asia, and Australia. From forensic scrutiny of promoter Agreements for Sale to aggressive litigation before TNRERA in Chennai, we protect your overseas capital with rigorous statutory enforcement.
                        </p>
                    </div>
