                        <p>
                            Filing a real estate complaint requires precise jurisdictional selection under the Tamil Nadu RERA Rules to prevent procedural dismissal or delays:
                        </p>
                        <div class="mb-3">
                            <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark-navy mb-1"><i class="fas fa-file-contract text-gold me-2"></i> Form M — Complaint to the Regulatory Authority</h4>
                            <p class="small text-muted mb-0">
                                Instituted under Section 31 before the TNRERA bench in Chennai. Applicable when seeking statutory directions against the promoter — such as fast-tracking project completion, releasing possession with Occupancy Certificate, obtaining sanctions, or directing payment of monthly interest on delay under Section 18.
